  ('iim-kozhikode', 'naac_grade', 'secondary', 'Not NAAC-graded', 'IIM Kozhikode''s accreditation page lists AMBA (since 2010) and EQUIS (since 2021, renewed 2024) accreditation and an AACSB application in progress, and no NAAC grade. A NAAC ''A+'' appears only on third-party listings, which cite no source.', 'IIM Kozhikode — Accreditation & Ranking', 'https://www.iimk.ac.in/accreditation-and-ranking', null, null),
  ('isi-delhi', 'total_students', 'estimate', 'About 140–200 degree students in 2026-27 (B.SDS, M.Stat first year, M.Math and MS (QE)), plus PhD/JRF research scholars.', 'ISI''s Prospectus 2026-27 gives the Delhi Centre 25 B.SDS seats a year (started 2024, so three batches), 35 MS (QE) seats a year (two batches), 18 M.Math seats (first batch) and the first year of the 38-seat M.Stat — about 200 students if every seat is filled. ISI''s Annual Report 2024-25 shows enrolment below the seat count (41 MS (QE) students joined against 56 seats), so the lower end allows for that. ISI files one NIRF return for all its centres, so there is no official Delhi-only figure.', 'ISI Prospectus 2026-27', 'https://admission.isical.ac.in/Documents/IsiAdmission2026/ISI-Prospectus-2026-27.pdf', '140', '200'),
  ('isi-delhi', 'enrollment', 'estimate', 'About 140–200 degree students at the Delhi Centre in 2026-27, up from roughly 100–140 in 2024-25 as the B.SDS batches (from 2024) and the M.Math batch (from 2026) were added.', 'Worked out from the Delhi Centre''s seats in ISI''s prospectus and the programmes ISI''s annual reports list for Delhi (M.Stat and MS (QE) throughout; B.SDS from 2024-25; M.Math from 2026-27). ISI reports student strength to NIRF only for the whole institute (1,241 students in 2024-25).', 'ISI Prospectus 2026-27', 'https://admission.isical.ac.in/Documents/IsiAdmission2026/ISI-Prospectus-2026-27.pdf', '140', '200'),
  ('isi-delhi', 'placements', 'estimate', 'Expected median of about ₹15–20 lakh a year for M.Stat and MS (QE) graduates who take jobs; a large share go on to PhDs instead.', 'ISI''s own figures for the same programmes at Kolkata in 2024-25: M.Stat 38 of 38 job-seekers placed, median ₹20 lakh (highest ₹50 lakh); MS (QE) 10 of 10, median ₹15.5 lakh (Annual Report 2024-25). ISI''s NIRF 2026 return gives a ₹22.5 lakh median for all its two-year PG graduates of 2024-25. ISI Delhi''s placement page could not be reached and no Delhi-only figures are published.', 'ISI Annual Report 2024-25', 'https://www.isical.ac.in/isical_web/files/about/publications/annual-reports/Annual_Report_2024-25.pdf', '1500000', '2000000')
